# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_l.tlk - bulk Surface push L: replies to an answer, a laugh, a
# yes and a no (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool act, no
# guard change. Rule names end in _ul. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.answer.ul1 act: backchannel
  "Ah, okay. That makes sense, thanks for explaining."
  "Good to know. I'll keep that in mind next time."
  "Mm, right. I see what you mean now."
  "Got it. That clears up a few things for me."
  "Ah, interesting. Thanks for the straight answer."
  "Okay, that's helpful. I'd been unsure about it."
  "Right, makes sense. Thanks for being clear."
  "Good answer. Short, sweet, and to the point."
@rule core.answer.ul2 act: agree
  "Yes, that's exactly what I'd have said."
  "Right, I think you've got it spot on."
  "Exactly. I'd have answered the same way, really."
  "Agreed. That's the most sensible thing I've heard today."
@rule core.answer.ul3 act: ask_about
  "And what made you think of that, out of curiosity?"
  "Okay, and how did that work out in the end?"
  "Wait, does that mean you've tried it before?"
  "So what's next, then? What's the plan?"
@rule core.answer.ul4 act: tell
  "That reminds me of something from last week, actually."
  "Funny, I had a similar thing happen just yesterday."
  "I had a bit of a run-in with that too, a while back."
@rule core.answer.ul5 act: disagree
  "Hm, I'd have guessed differently, but it's your call."
  "I'm not sure about that. I'd want to check first."
@rule core.answer.ul6 act: joke
  "Wow, that's a very confident answer. I'm impressed."
  "Good answer. I'd give it a gold star and a biscuit."
  "That's the most dramatic answer I've ever been given. Brilliant."
@rule core.answer.ul7 act: tease
  "Of course that's your answer. Nobody else would say it."
  "Well, that's a clever way of putting it. Show-off."
@rule core.answer.ul8 act: laugh
  "Ha! That's a surprising answer, but I like it."
  "Hee, I didn't see that one coming at all."
@rule core.laugh.ul1 act: laugh
  "Ha! I can't stop now, that was too good."
  "Hee hee, you're contagious. I'm still giggling."
  "Ha, okay, okay. You win. For now."
  "Hah! I'm laughing at myself, so thanks for that."
@rule core.laugh.ul2 act: joke
  "Okay, I'll keep the jokes coming. You're a good audience."
  "Thanks, I'll be here all week. Bring snacks."
  "Good, I like a crowd that laughs. Makes it worthwhile."
@rule core.laugh.ul3 act: tease
  "Look at you, laughing at my expense. Rude but fair."
  "You've got a very loud laugh, did you know that?"
@rule core.laugh.ul4 act: complain
  "Stop laughing, I'm trying to be serious over here!"
  "It's not that funny. Okay, it's a little funny."
@rule core.laugh.ul5 act: backchannel
  "Glad you're enjoying yourself. It's infectious, that laugh."
  "Nice to hear. I like it when you're in a good mood."
@rule core.yes.ul1 act: backchannel
  "Good, that's settled then. Thanks for saying so."
  "Okay, yes. I'll take that as a firm answer."
  "Yes, right. Good to have that cleared up."
@rule core.yes.ul2 act: thank
  "Thanks, I'm glad you agreed. That helps a lot."
  "Thank you. I hoped you'd say yes to that."
@rule core.yes.ul3 act: joke
  "Yes! Quick, before you change your mind."
  "Yes, and I'll hold you to it. Not a joke."
@rule core.yes.ul4 act: agree
  "Yes, I'm with you on that. Let's go."
  "Yes. Definitely. We agree, which is a rare treat."
@rule core.no.ul1 act: backchannel
  "Okay, no problem. Maybe another time."
  "Fair enough. I'll ask again when it's a better day."
  "No? Alright, I understand. Thanks for telling me."
@rule core.no.ul2 act: complain
  "No? Ugh, I was hoping you'd say yes this time."
  "Aw, no? That's a bit of a letdown, honestly."
@rule core.no.ul3 act: joke
  "No? That's a crushing blow. I'll recover, probably."
  "No, huh? Your loss. More snacks for me."
@rule core.no.ul4 act: disagree
  "I see it differently, but I'll respect your no."
  "Hm, no. I'd have said yes, but it's your choice."
